  "body": "The fact that we stored the actual object was just for specification\nconvenience, but had observable consequences by demanding that the same\nobject be exposed repeatedly. Cloning allows a bit more implementation\nflexibility.\n\n/cc @whatwg/modules. Tests will come from Chrome; in https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/698467 we noted this requirement was too strict and so held off writing tests for it, so now we'll write tests for the opposite (i.e. that they are always distinct).\n\n\n<!--\n    This comment and the below content is programatically generated.\n    You may add a comma-separated list of anchors you'd like a\n    direct link to below (e.g. #idl-serializers, #idl-sequence):\n\n    Don't remove this comment or modify anything below this line.\n    If you don't want a preview generated for this pull request,\n    just replace the whole of this comment's content by \"no preview\"\n    and remove what's below.\n-->\n***\n\n### :boom: Error: Wattsi server error :boom: ###\n\n[PR Preview](https://github.com/tobie/pr-preview#pr-preview) failed to build. _(Last tried on Jan 15, 2021, 7:58 AM UTC)_.\n\n<details>\n<summary>More</summary>\n\n\nPR Preview relies on a number of web services to run. There seems to be an issue with the following one:\n\n:rotating_light: [Wattsi Server](https://github.com/domenic/wattsi-server) - Wattsi Server is the web service used to build the WHATWG HTML spec.\n\n:link: [Related URL](https://build.whatwg.org/wattsi)\n\n```\nCommand failed: /home/noderunner/wattsi/bin/wattsi /tmp/upload_b18f17294e385771c4fd20018f4e1187 (sha not provided) 3lqdkahtuhb default /tmp/upload_3ea4522c0b4cbbba4c0adaf1b40da861\n\n```\n\n_If you don't have enough information above to solve the error by yourself (or to understand to which web service the error is related to, if any), please [file an issue](https://github.com/tobie/pr-preview/issues/new?title=Error%20not%20surfaced%20properly&body=See%20whatwg/html%233318.)._\n</details>\n",
